      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-26T16:03:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So this is applying the VM DTBO to an empty DT: can you remind me why we needed to pass an overlay to pvmfw (from ABL) instead of a regular DT?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 82,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 82,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "5b081cabf23717fd891b23ffee2533801422ca98",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2cd96aa6_75c14833",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/devices.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 82,
      "author": {
        "id": 1019013
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-27T16:10:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s no desperate reason here; we keep the VM devices in VM DTBO in host DT, and simply copied it from the `ABL`.\n\nWould you prefer ABL to provide overlaid VM DTBO in `pvmfw`\u0027s config? I\u0027m OK with it (and Jiyong as well). But my concern is debug policy.\n\nIf we get overlaid VM DTBO, then I feel bad if debug policy works differently. But unfortunately we already released the debug policy guideline and it\u0027s breaking change.\n\nSo here are options from top of my head:\n\nOption 1) Just get VM DTBO from ABL (i.e. keep it as-is)\n\nOption 2) New `pvmfw` config (`v1.1`) takes debug policy DTBO while VM DTBO should be provided as overlaid. (i.e. format differs between debug policy DTBO and VM DTBO)\n\nOption 3) New `pvmfw` config (`v1.1`) isn\u0027t compatible with older version (`v1.0`)-- it takes overlaid debug policy and VM DTBO. VM DTBO can be mandatory.\n\nOption 4) New `pvmfw` config (`v1.1`) supports both overlay DT and overlaid DT. Heuristic is needed to distinguish between two. (perhaps search for `__overlay__`?)\n\n\nWhat do you think? If ABL sends overlaid VM DTBO, then we don\u0027t need `OwnedFdt` nor applying overlay for every VM boot.",
      "parentUuid": "3ed0d7b0_16dd862b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 82,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 82,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "5b081cabf23717fd891b23ffee2533801422ca98",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "25cc5799_5d430b5c",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/devices.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 82,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-29T09:04:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Would you prefer ABL to provide overlaid VM DTBO in pvmfw\u0027s config?\n\nIf we\u0027re only ever going to use it as a DT (not DTBO), yes, as it will avoid increasing pVM boots for no reason. But back to my original question: wasn\u0027t there a reason for it to be a DTBO? Something to do with needing it to map the VM DTBO nodes to their respective targeted guest DT node? Or following phandles? I can\u0027t remember ...\n\n\u003e If we get overlaid VM DTBO, then I feel bad if debug policy works differently.\n\nThose are different and I don\u0027t believe we should look for any symmetry: the DP DTBO is intended to be applied by pvmfw to the DT so is naturally an overlay. OTOH, the VM DTBO is only ever consulted as a trusted reference.",
      "parentUuid": "2cd96aa6_75c14833",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 82,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 82,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "5b081cabf23717fd891b23ffee2533801422ca98",
