      "writtenOn": "2023-09-26T16:03:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This absolutely doesn\u0027t work as the guest kernel binds against nodes (mostly) based on their `\u003ccompatible\u003e` property and actually (mostly) ignores their names so a malicious host could abuse this implementation by giving its malicious nodes names from `CROSVM_NODES`, effectively bypassing their validation you\u0027re adding. Note how `patch_device_tree` ignored nodes path. For example, would it make sense to validate (and mark for being carried over) any node that has the `\u003candroid,pvmfw,...\u003e` properties and their dependencies?",
